=== the half of this bond the build repo cannot carry ===
  bc_docstring_lists_eight_kinds     True
  noslip_negates_momentum            True
  wall_reads_T_wall                  True
  wall_reads_no_slip_mask            True
  no_wall_velocity_param             True

  So a gas agent can SUPPLY a traction -- it has the wall pressure --
  and cannot RESPOND to a velocity: there is no channel to impose one.
  The MECH bond at every gas-solid seam in this graph is one-sided by
  a MISSING CAPABILITY, and a declaration cannot see the difference
  between that and a modelling choice. W97 found a field-to-lumped
  MECH seam one-sided by Re_h; this is one-sided by a boundary
  condition that does not exist.

=== the load the projection removes, which is the trajectory's input ===
  the rigid-load map d(V^T f)/d(traction) is 3 x 14
  singular values: 2.838828e-03, 4.595940e-04, 3.337581e-05
  rank 3 -- the seam window drives all three planar modes, the
  torque one 85.1x more weakly than the leading translation.

  V is orthonormal to 1.89e-15
  at a UNIFORM ambient traction the net rigid load is [ 0.0000e+00 -7.4607e-14  1.3840e-01]
  -- the two FORCES cancel to machine precision and the TORQUE does
  not. That is right and it is the shell's thickness talking: the
  inner and outer faces have equal projected area, so a uniform
  pressure exerts no net force, but they sit at different radii, so
  it exerts a COUPLE. The trajectory must receive that couple and the
  structure must not, which is precisely what the projection does.

